    </answer>
    <solution><p>Solution</p>
<p>The coordinates of a point are the pair (x,y) where x is the distance to the
right</p>
<p>of the y axis (which is negative if the point is to the left of the
y axis)</p>
<p>and y is the distance above the x axis.</p>
<p>For example, the point with coordinates (2,1) is 2 unit to the right of the y axis</p>
<p>and 3 units above the x axis, so it is the point A.</p>
</solution>
